---
name: trick-secret-runtime
description: |-
  Review existing tricks after the standard secret-runtime contract was added.
  For every trick, inspect its code and declare any credential dependency in a
  sibling secrets.json so bbx trick can provide the granted value at launch.
  This is an agent-applied migration because only the trick author can decide
  whether an external API needs a secret.
steps:
  - id: review-tricks
    description: Review every existing trick for secret dependencies
    precheck:
      shells:
        - |-
          if ! find src/tricks/scripts -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 2 -name index.ts -print -quit 2>/dev/null | grep -q .; then
            echo "No tricks found — nothing to migrate."
            exit $CHECK_SKIP
          fi
          f="_config/migration-runs/trick-secret-runtime.checklist.md"
          if test -f "$f" && ! grep -q '\[ \]' "$f" && bbx trick --check-secrets >/dev/null 2>&1; then
            echo "Trick secret review is already complete."
            exit $CHECK_SKIP
          fi
          echo "Existing tricks require secret-dependency review."
        whys:
          - Every existing trick has been reviewed, declarations validate, and the checklist is complete.
    run:
      agents:
        - prompt: |-
            Review every existing trick under src/tricks/scripts/. This migration
            is about the new standard secret runtime: `bbx trick <name>` reads a
            sibling `secrets.json`, resolves each declared grant at launch, and
            injects the value only into that trick process.

            For each trick, inspect index.ts and its imports. If it calls an
            external service that requires a credential, create or update the
            sibling `secrets.json` with the secret name, the short lowercase
            reason for using it, and the environment variable the code reads:

            [{"name":"openai-images","reason":"image-generation","env":"OPENAI_API_KEY"}]

            Do not guess a secret name or alter the machine store. If the
            dependency is unclear, leave the trick unchanged and record the
            uncertainty in the checklist for the boxholder. Never put a value
            in the trick, a file, argv, or a log.

            Maintain this checklist at
            `_config/migration-runs/trick-secret-runtime.checklist.md`. Create
            it with exactly these items and change `- [ ]` to `- [x]` only when
            genuinely complete, appending a short note with file paths:

            - [ ] Listed every existing trick under `src/tricks/scripts/`.
            - [ ] Inspected every trick's code and imports for credentialed external services.
            - [ ] Added or updated `secrets.json` for every confirmed credential dependency.
            - [ ] Left no secret values in source, arguments, files, or logs.
            - [ ] Ran `bbx trick --check-secrets` and resolved every declaration error.

            Do not check an item you did not complete. When all items are
            checked and the validation command passes, you are done.
          max-turns: 40
    validate:
      shells:
        - bbx trick --check-secrets
        - |-
          f="_config/migration-runs/trick-secret-runtime.checklist.md"
          test -f "$f" && grep -q '\[x\]' "$f" && ! grep -q '\[ \]' "$f"
      severity: abort
      instructions:
        - Every existing trick was reviewed and confirmed credential dependencies have valid declarations.
      whys:
        - The migration completes only after the agent's review checklist and machine declaration validation both pass.
